I don't think that a set of rigidly enforced "very simple" rules will work.
 For example, what happens to someone's property when that someone dies? 
The Blue Goo needs to enforce concepts like fiduciary, executor, and
probate court.  What about property owned by corporations?  To take a
larger perspective on the problem, what happens when society changes and
people want new concepts of property?  Are they to be limited to the rules
set up by the designers of the Blue Goo?  

