as complex and ever-changing as the existing legal system.  The existing
system is certainly complex enough to run "hostile programs"; such programs
are more normally called "unjust loopholes".  Clever
programmers^H^H^H^H^H^H^H^H lawyers are well-paid to devise them.  

I have talked to Eric Drexler about this.  His idea at the time was that
the legal system would be operated entirely by superhuman AI judges.  That
was a while ago, though.  I don't know what his thinking on the matter is
now.


